 "law": "Scandlines' gross freight tariffs per single crossing, excluding VAT, loaded (Germany–Denmark from 10 m, valid from 2026-01-01; small units to 9 m, valid from 2026-01-01; transit Germany–Sweden North, valid from 2026-01-01), and Øresundslinjen's freight tariff Helsingør–Helsingborg (2026-01-01 to 2026-12-31: trucks to 8 m EUR 91.4, to 13 m EUR 145.9, to 16 m EUR 157.9, to 26 m EUR 169.3); by the truck's length in whole metres up. With the surcharges per commencing metre (at least 7) as from 2026-04-01: Puttgarden–Rødby BAF 1.15 and GIR 0.88, Rostock–Gedser BAF 3.1 and GIR 1.66, Helsingør–Helsingborg energy 1.22 and green 0.47 EUR. Scandlines' ETS surcharge (0.17 and 0.63 EUR per metre) isn't added: carbon-cost prices the EU ETS on a crossing from the ships' MRV data. A trip over Puttgarden–Rødby or Rostock–Gedser and Helsingør–Helsingborg pays the transit ticket. Over-length (over 26 m), over-width and over-weight surcharges aren't applied. Ports at OpenStreetMap's ferry terminals, priced where the line goes out on its car ferry line.",
